.terraform/
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. HashiCorp's guidance is to
# commit it: the provider constraints here are ~> ranges, so without the lock a
# fresh clone resolves whatever the registry serves that day and two operators
# can apply the same code against different provider builds. It also records the
# checksums that make a provider swap detectable.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!terraform.tfvars.example
crash.log
